  "verbalization": "Verapamil is implicated in the interaction with the CD276 antigen through a series of molecular pathways involving ATP-binding cassette sub-family G member 1 (ABCG1). The evidence suggests that Verapamil acts as a target for multiple compounds, including [(2E,5R,8S)-2-hexa-2,4-diynylidene-1,10-dioxaspiro[4.5]dec-3-en-8-yl] acetate, 3'-O-methyltricetin 3-O-alpha-L-rhamnopyranoside, and Rutin, all of which are known to target CD276. This indicates that Verapamil may exert its biological effects through a common mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of ABCG1, which is a key player in drug efflux and has been shown to interact with CD276 in various cellular contexts. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Verapamil to influence CD276-dependent processes, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
